692. Top K Frequent Words
Given an array of strings words and an integer k, return the k most frequent strings.
Return the answer sorted by the frequency from highest to lowest. Sort the words with the same frequency by their lexicographical order.

Example 1:
Input: words = ["i","love","leetcode","i","love","coding"], k = 2
Output: ["i","love"]
Explanation: "i" and "love" are the two most frequent words.
Note that "i" comes before "love" due to a lower alphabetical order.

Example 2:
Input: words = ["the","day","is","sunny","the","the","the","sunny","is","is"], k = 4
Output: ["the","is","sunny","day"]
Explanation: "the", "is", "sunny" and "day" are the four most frequent words, with the number of occurrence being 4, 3, 2 and 1 respectively.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithm (Top K Frequent Words – Heap Method):

1) Create a TreeMap to store frequency of each word.
2) Traverse the input array and count frequency of each word.
3) Create a PriorityQueue (max-heap) where:
4) Words with higher frequency have higher priority.
5) If two words have same frequency, lexicographically smaller word comes first.
6) Insert all (word, frequency) pairs into the heap.
7) Remove top k elements from the heap and store their words in the result list.
8) Return the result list.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIRST LEVEL CODE: TIME COMPLEXITY:O(N + K log K) || SPACE COMPLEXITY:O(K) 
class Pair{
    private String word;
    private int values;
    Pair(String wrd,int val)
    {
        this.word=wrd;
        this.values=val;
    }
    public String getWord(){
        return word;
    }
    public int getValue(){
        return values;
    }
}
class Solution {
    public List<String> topKFrequent(String[] words, int k) {
        Map<String,Integer> mapp=new TreeMap<>();
        PriorityQueue<Pair> pq=new PriorityQueue<>((a,b) -> {
            if(a.getValue() == b.getValue()){
                return a.getWord().compareTo(b.getWord());
            }
            else
            {
                return b.getValue() - a.getValue();
            }
});
        List<String> result=new ArrayList<>();
        for(int i=0;i<words.length;i++)
        {
            if(mapp.containsKey(words[i]))
            {
                mapp.put(words[i],(mapp.get(words[i])+1));
            }
            else
            {
                mapp.put(words[i],1);
            }
        }
        for(Map.Entry<String,Integer> entry : mapp.entrySet())
        {
            pq.add(new Pair(entry.getKey(),entry.getValue()));
        }
        for(int i=0;i<k;i++)
        {
            result.add(pq.poll().getWord());
        }
        return result;
    }
}
